ORIGINAL REQUEST:
We need to roll up daily airline cabin quality-assurance inspections into a single daily summary for Australia and New Zealand operations. Metadata and sample rows are below (sorted by audit_day):

<Metadata id="CabinQaLog">
  <Record name="QaObservation" fieldDelimiter="|">
    <Field name="audit_day" type="date" dateFormat="yyyy-MM-dd" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="sectors_checked" type="long" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="cabin_findings" type="integer" nullable="true"/>
  </Record>
</Metadata>

<Metadata id="QaDaySummary">
  <Record name="QaDailyRollup" fieldDelimiter="|">
    <Field name="audit_day" type="date"/>
    <Field name="total_sectors_checked" type="long"/>
    <Field name="avg_findings_per_sector" type="decimal" scale="4" nullable="true"/>
    <Field name="min_findings_rate" type="decimal" scale="4" nullable="true"/>
    <Field name="max_findings_rate" type="decimal" scale="4" nullable="true"/>
  </Record>
</Metadata>

Sample data:
audit_day|sectors_checked|cabin_findings
2026-02-14|18|5
2026-02-14|12|
2026-02-14|10|1
2026-02-15|20|4

Use a Rollup component grouping by audit_day. Compute total_sectors_checked as the sum of sectors_checked across all rows for the day.

For rate-based measures, only use rows where cabin_findings is not null and sectors_checked > 0. For each usable row, its findings rate is cabin_findings / sectors_checked.

Compute avg_findings_per_sector as total cabin_findings divided by total sectors_checked over usable rows for the day, rounded to 4 decimals using banker's rounding. Compute minimum and maximum of the per-row findings rate across usable rows. If a day has no usable rows, set avg_findings_per_sector, min_findings_rate, and max_findings_rate to null.

Use an accumulator metadata class named QaAcc with these fields:
- long allSectorSum
- long usableSectorSum
- integer findingsSum
- decimal minRate
- decimal maxRate
- integer usableRowCnt

Please provide CTL2 code for the Rollup: initGroup, updateGroup, finishGroup, and transform functions. Also state which field is the group key and show the expected accumulator structure (as above) in the response.

PROPOSED CTL2 IMPLEMENTATION:
```ctl
//#CTL2

// Group key: audit_day
// Accumulator metadata QaAcc:
// - long allSectorSum
// - long usableSectorSum
// - integer findingsSum
// - decimal minRate
// - decimal maxRate
// - integer usableRowCnt

function void initGroup(QaAcc acc) {
    acc.allSectorSum = 0L;
    acc.usableSectorSum = 0L;
    acc.findingsSum = 0;
    acc.minRate = null;
    acc.maxRate = null;
    acc.usableRowCnt = 0;
    return;
}

function boolean updateGroup(QaAcc acc) {
    acc.allSectorSum += $in.0.sectors_checked;

    if (!isnull($in.0.cabin_findings) && $in.0.sectors_checked > 0L) {
        decimal rate = $in.0.cabin_findings / $in.0.sectors_checked;

        acc.usableSectorSum += $in.0.sectors_checked;
        acc.findingsSum += $in.0.cabin_findings;

        if (acc.usableRowCnt == 0) {
            acc.minRate = rate;
            acc.maxRate = rate;
        } else {
            if (rate < acc.minRate) acc.minRate = rate;
            if (rate > acc.maxRate) acc.maxRate = rate;
        }

        acc.usableRowCnt++;
    }

    return true;
}

function boolean finishGroup(QaAcc acc) {
    return true;
}

function integer updateTransform(integer counter, QaAcc acc) {
    return SKIP;
}

function integer transform(integer counter, QaAcc acc) {
    if (counter > 0) return SKIP;

    $out.0.audit_day = $in.0.audit_day;
    $out.0.total_sectors_checked = acc.allSectorSum;

    if (acc.usableRowCnt == 0) {
        $out.0.avg_findings_per_sector = null;
        $out.0.min_findings_rate = null;
        $out.0.max_findings_rate = null;
    } else {
        $out.0.avg_findings_per_sector =
            roundHalfToEven(acc.findingsSum / acc.usableSectorSum, 4);
        $out.0.min_findings_rate = acc.minRate;
        $out.0.max_findings_rate = acc.maxRate;
    }

    return OK;
}
```

