Business logic:
- Missing PatientCover or ProcedureTariff produces REVIEW with zero amounts. Use PATIENT_COVER_NOT_FOUND when both are missing or when PatientCover alone is missing; otherwise use PROCEDURE_TARIFF_NOT_FOUND.
- After those checks, produce REVIEW with COVER_OR_REFERRAL_CHECK when either cover_status is not ELIGIBLE, or referral_needed is true and referral_reference is null.
- A payer scheme is valid only when its row exists, treatment_date is on or after valid_from, and either valid_until is null or treatment_date is on or before valid_until. An invalid payer scheme produces REVIEW with PAYER_SCHEME_INVALID.
- Otherwise, calculate the pre-VAT amount as unit_fee_eur times service_units plus consumables_eur, treating a null consumables_eur as zero. Calculate invoice_total_eur by applying vat_percentage to the pre-VAT amount. Calculate payer_amount_eur as invoice_total_eur times reimbursement_percentage divided by 100, and patient_amount_eur as invoice_total_eur minus payer_amount_eur. Round each amount to two decimals. Set invoice_status to ISSUED and review_reason to null.

