- Lookup table ID: SouthAsiaFoodRiskLookup.
- Lookup record metadata: FoodRiskRule(nation_key:string, municipality_prefix:string, baseline_fee_rate:decimal, packaged_food_rate:decimal, high_risk_rate:decimal, rule_start:date, rule_end:date nullable="true").
- Key fields are nation_key and municipality_prefix. Several records may share a nation_key; choose the matching record whose municipality_prefix is the longest prefix of municipal_code and whose rule date range includes audit_date. A null rule_end has no end date.

Output metadata: ComplianceAuditOut(filing_reference:string, supervising_authority:string, applied_fee_rate:decimal, compliance_fee:decimal, audit_disposition:string).

Business logic:
- If no matching lookup record exists, set supervising_authority to PENDING_REVIEW, applied_fee_rate and compliance_fee to zero, and audit_disposition to MANUAL_CHECK.
- Otherwise, supervising_authority is market_nation plus : plus municipality_prefix.
- Use high_risk_rate when refrigeration_alert is true OR food_category starts with RAW_. Otherwise, use packaged_food_rate when food_category contains READY_TO_EAT; use baseline_fee_rate for all remaining food_category values.
- A null selected fee rate is zero. compliance_fee is declared_consignment_value multiplied by applied_fee_rate divided by 100, rounded to two decimals.
- Set audit_disposition to ESCALATE when refrigeration_alert is true and compliance_fee is greater than zero. Set it to WAIVED when compliance_fee is zero; otherwise set it to CLEARED.

