Input metadata: WorkshopVisitIn(visit_reference:string, market:string, member_number:string, qualifying_spend:decimal, programme_tier:string, workshop_date:date, low_emission_vehicle:boolean).
The member_number and workshop_date fields may be null.

Lookup table definition:
- Lookup table ID: MotoringRewardsLookup.
- Lookup record metadata: RewardScheme(market_code:string, tier_code:string, points_per_currency:decimal, visit_points_cap:long, low_emission_bonus:long, campaign_begins:date, campaign_ends:date, points_validity_days:integer).
- Key fields are market_code and tier_code; at most one record matches.

Port 0 metadata: RewardAwardOut(visit_reference:string, earned_points:long, bonus_points:long, points_expiry_date:date, reward_band:string).
Port 1 metadata: VisitReviewOut(visit_reference:string, review_reason:string, qualifying_spend:decimal).

Business logic:
- Look up the reward scheme using market and programme_tier. If no scheme matches, send port 1 with review_reason REWARD_SCHEME_UNAVAILABLE.
- When a scheme exists, send port 1 with review_reason INCOMPLETE_MEMBER_VISIT if member_number is null or workshop_date is null.
- Otherwise, send port 1 with review_reason OUTSIDE_REWARD_CAMPAIGN if qualifying_spend is zero or below, or if workshop_date is before campaign_begins or after campaign_ends.
- For all other visits, earned_points is the lower of the whole-number result of qualifying_spend multiplied by points_per_currency and visit_points_cap. bonus_points is low_emission_bonus only when low_emission_vehicle is true and earned_points is positive; otherwise it is zero.
- points_expiry_date is workshop_date plus points_validity_days. reward_band is PREMIUM when earned_points plus bonus_points is at least 2,500; otherwise it is STANDARD. Send these records to port 0.

