Business logic:
- Retrieve the market onboarding policy using market_iso. If no policy exists, use settlement currency `USD`, a minimum monthly revenue of 0, 5 follow-up days, a maximum facility percentage of 20, and no excluded trade prefixes. onboarding_reference is market_iso + '-' + application_ref. registered_name is enterprise_name trimmed and converted to upper case.
- approved_facility_amount is based on the policy facility ceiling, calculated as average_monthly_revenue multiplied by maximum_facility_pct divided by 100. When requested_facility_amount is non-null, greater than zero, and no greater than that calculated ceiling, use requested_facility_amount; otherwise use the calculated ceiling. Round the result to two decimals.
- business_maturity is UNKNOWN when incorporation_date is null. Otherwise it is STARTUP when incorporation_date is less than 365 days before the current graph date, MULTI_OUTLET when outlet_count is greater than 1, and ESTABLISHED otherwise.
- contact_details_json, when supplied, is a JSON object that can contain string keys primary_phone and notification_email. Parse it and map those keys. Missing JSON, missing keys, null values, malformed JSON, or a value that is not a JSON object must produce null primary_phone/notification_email without failing the transform.
- An enterprise is contactable when at least one of primary_phone or notification_email is non-null and not an empty string after trimming.
- An application is REJECTED when trade_classification begins with any excluded_trade_prefixes value, or when incorporation_date is later than the current graph date. It is NEEDS_INFORMATION when it is not rejected and either identity_verification_date is null or the enterprise is not contactable. It is MANUAL_REVIEW when it is neither rejected nor missing information and average_monthly_revenue is less than the policy minimum_monthly_revenue. Otherwise it is APPROVED.
- decision_reason is EXCLUDED_TRADE when the application is rejected because of an excluded trade prefix, FUTURE_INCORPORATION_DATE when it is rejected because incorporation_date is in the future, MISSING_CONTACT_OR_IDENTITY when the decision is NEEDS_INFORMATION, and REVENUE_BELOW_MARKET_MINIMUM when the decision is MANUAL_REVIEW. It is null for APPROVED applications. When more than one rejection condition applies, EXCLUDED_TRADE takes precedence.
- next_action_date is the current graph date for REJECTED and APPROVED applications, the current graph date plus twice follow_up_days for NEEDS_INFORMATION applications, and the current graph date plus follow_up_days for MANUAL_REVIEW applications. Emit one record.

